 "text": "Hey, good to have you back. How are you? That's a great plan. Which area do you live in? Okay. Hold. A small white bird with a thin bill. It nests in the big oak across the street, and it' been feeding on the burr and the garden all winter. It' probably a common blackbird. If it were, the bird would usually land on the ground near you. That's very sensible. A basic guide is enough for that. Just remember that some berries are safe even after they're ripe.",
